. Is this a daycare setting with toys/play equipment visible?**  \n✅ **Yes.**  \nThe “DAYCARE” sign is visible in Frames 4–11. Inside (Frames 15–30), there are colorful mats, toys, and child-sized furniture — consistent with a daycare environment.\n\n---\n\n**5. Is this the first exercise activity shown with infants?**  \n❌ **No.**  \nThe **first activity** shown with the infants is **storytime**, not exercise.  \nThe “Hands-up” motion (Frame 8–11) is **not an exercise led by the teacher** — she is not facing the infants, nor are they mimicking her. It is not structured or instructional.  \nTherefore, **no exercise activity is shown before the storytime**, making “Hands-up” not the first exercise.\n\n---\n\n**6. Is the teacher leading a physical activity with infants?**  \n❌ **No — not in the first activity.**  \nThe teacher’s first interaction with the infants is **sedentary** — she sits on a cabinet and reads to them.  \nThe “Hands-up” motion (Frame 8–11) is **not led by her** — she is turning away, and the infants are not participating. It is not a guided physical activity.\n\n---\n\n### Final Assessment:\n\n- The **first activity** the substitute teacher does with the infants is **reading a story**, not any physical exercise.\n- The “Hands-up” motion (Frame 8–11) is **not led by the teacher**, **not performed with the infants**, and **not an exercise** in context.\n- Therefore, **option 2 (“Hands-up”) is incorrect**.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Correct Answer: Not 2. The first activity is storytime, not “Hands-up”.**\n\nThe correct answer should reflect the **first instructed activity** — which is **storytelling**, not physical exercise. If “Hands-up” is the only exercise option, then **none of the exercise options are correct** for the “first” activity."}, {'batch_start': 60, 'batch_end': 81, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1545.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1546.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lv